# Smoke Test Coverage Standards

## Every scenario must cover these 5 checks
1. Server startup responds
2. Homepage loads without console errors  
3. At least 3 routes checked for correct status codes
4. At least 1 API endpoint verified
5. No 5xx errors in the route matrix

## Reporter output must be machine-readable
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — structured JSON on stdout
const result: SmokeResult = {
  passed: allChecksPassed,
  durationMs: totalTime,
  failures: failedChecks.map(c => ({ check: c.name, reason: c.error })),
  summary: `${passed}/${total} checks passed`,
};
console.log(JSON.stringify(result));

// ❌ BAD — human text on stdout
console.log("All tests passed! Great job.");
```

## Scenarios are configuration, not test logic
Keep business logic in `src/checks/`. Scenarios should only configure which checks to run and with what parameters.

## 60-second budget
If a smoke suite takes more than 60 seconds, it has too many checks. Add to integration tests instead.
